{"title":"Descent","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Given a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Permutation\" title=\"Permutation\">permutation</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/169768b4fdb88eba4037a3903b362a3d08f9c3d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w = w_1 w_2 \\cdots w_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"133\" height=\"18\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/741b0d455066ae83b72e54352f8558639b172e3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1, 2, \\ldots, n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> is said to have a <b>descent</b> at position <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/2/af2f357d0a947bd575fc0a0a7b7c6bd7c4be04d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w_i &gt; w_{i + 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" />.  For example, the permutation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/8/718f585182a2d8a220d0831180a40d02ef3f4ad0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15243$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" /> has descents at positions 2 (since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/d/c8d5bdad42b66356725c7df289a36023363f2ede.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 &gt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />) and 4 (since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e963b000c165a05ed41b3b5f8ac5d1e8b6ce12a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 &gt; 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />).\n</p><p>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Set\" title=\"Set\">set</a> of descents of a permutation is called its <i>descent set.</i>  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> is a permutation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/741b0d455066ae83b72e54352f8558639b172e3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1, 2, \\ldots, n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" /> then its descent set is some subset of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f6dfe735808b77939faabb2f5a1ed8d67e745b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1, 2, \\ldots, n - 1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" />.  \n</p><p><br />\n<i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Descent&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018082501\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.009 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.014 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 40/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 262/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1994/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.011      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    6.011      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:8310:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018082501 and revision id 32571. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}